.page cut 1 select parts of each line

# SYNOPSIS
*cut* *-f* _LIST_ [*-d* _DELIM_] [*-s*] [*--output-delimiter*=_STR_] [_FILE_...]
*cut* *-c* _LIST_ [_FILE_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`cut` writes the selected parts of every line of its input (standard input if no file is named).

A _LIST_ is made of numbers and ranges separated by commas: `3`, `2-5`, `4-` (from 4 to the end), `-3` (up to 3), `1,5-7`. Positions start at 1.

# OPTIONS
@ *-f* _LIST_
    Select fields. The default field separator is the tab character. A line without the separator is passed through unchanged, unless `-s` is used.
@ *-d* _DELIM_
    Use the first character of _DELIM_ as the field separator.
@ *-s*
    With `-f`, drop lines that do not contain the separator.
@ *--output-delimiter*=_STR_
    Put _STR_ between the selected fields instead of the input separator.
@ *-c* _LIST_, *-b* _LIST_
    Select byte positions. (Characters are not distinguished from bytes: a multibyte UTF-8 character occupies several positions.)

# EXAMPLES
    cut -d: -f1,6 /Hakurei/etc/passwd
    cut -c1-8 listing.txt
    echo "a,b,c" | cut -d, -f2-
    cut -d: -f1 --output-delimiter=' / ' /Hakurei/etc/group

# SEE ALSO
paste(1), sort(1), tr(1)
